@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+"""QWEN36_SYNC_LEAN=1: opt-in removal of avoidable host<->GPU synchronizations on the forward path.
+
+Every change behind this flag keeps the GPU work bitwise identical (same model kernels on the same
+inputs in the same order); only host waiting and how metadata is produced change:
+
+  * FLA chunk metadata (``freetoken.kernel.fla.index``): the chunk index/offset tables of a
+    prefill forward are built from the host copy of ``cu_seqlens`` when the metadata is built and
+    seeded into the FLA tensor cache, instead of being derived on the first GDN layer from the
+    device tensor (one ``.tolist()`` read + two blocking copies = three full stream drains per
+    prefill chunk). Same int64 values. Likewise the CUDA GDN empty-sequence check
+    (``freetoken.kernel.cuda_gdn.has_empty_sequence``, one ``.item()`` drain per prefill chunk):
+    same expression on the same values, on the host copy.
+  * FlashInfer prefill plans under layer-major prefill (``freetoken.attention.fi`` +
+    ``freetoken.engine.layer_major``): one plan per chunk and window on a pooled per-chunk wrapper
+    (own int workspace / pinned staging / event) reused by every attention layer, instead of a
+    re-plan of the shared wrapper (with an event wait on the previous plan) for every
+    (attention layer, chunk) task. Same plan inputs -> same plan bytes. With grouped attention
+    (QWEN36_LAYER_MAJOR_ATTN_BATCH=k) every group gets its own pooled wrapper too (planned once
+    per window instead of once per grouped layer), and the member probes / k=1 fallbacks run on
+    the members' own pooled wrappers.
+  * MoE prefill double-buffer invalidation (``freetoken.moe.offload_cache``): the sync-free
+    masked_fill form also when layer-major prefill is off (it was already on with it).
+
+Read at call time (cheap), so tests can toggle it per case.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+
+_ON = {"1", "true", "yes", "on"}
+
+
+def enabled() -> bool:
+    return os.environ.get("QWEN36_SYNC_LEAN", "0").strip().lower() in _ON
+
+
+__all__ = ["enabled"]
